course: dictionary
lesson: 14864
title: Reabsorb: taking things back in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Re- means again, and absorb means to soak something up. So reabsorb means to take something back in after it has come out or been given off. «The dry sponge began to reabsorb the water we had squeezed out.» The sponge soaks the water up again.
explain: Your body does this too. «Your kidneys filter your blood and reabsorb the water and sugar it needs.» Only the waste leaves your body as urine, because the useful things were taken back into the blood.
explain: You can also use reabsorb for people and groups. «The team wants to reabsorb the players who left last year.» It means bring them back into the group they left. To check, swap in take back: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Re- at the start of a word means again.
fact: Reabsorb means to take something back in after it has come out or been given off.
fact: In science, the kidneys reabsorb useful things like water and glucose into the blood, so only waste leaves as urine.
fact: Plants and soil can also reabsorb water.
fact: A team or company can reabsorb people or workers who left it, bringing them back into the group.
exercise: «The kidneys reabsorb water and sugar.» What does reabsorb mean here? | To throw away for good | *To take back into the blood | To pass out as urine | To freeze solid
exercise: «The sponge began to reabsorb the spilled water.» What is the sponge doing? | Freezing the water | *Soaking up the water again | Pouring water out | Throwing the water away
exercise: What does the re- in reabsorb mean? | Away | Under | *Again | Not
test: «After the rain, the soil will reabsorb the water slowly.» What does reabsorb mean? | *To take water back in | To spill water on the ground | To make water boil | To pour away the rain
test: «The team wanted to reabsorb the player who had left.» What does this mean? | *To bring the player back into the team | To make the player run faster | To count the players in a line | To send the player away for good
exam: Which sentence shows the body taking a useful substance back into the blood? | «We ate pizza for lunch.» | «The dog barked at the postman.» | *«The kidneys reabsorb the sugar the body needs.» | «The bus was late again.»
